    "done_when": "A test in tests/test_roadmap.py builds two synthesised plans in a temporary docs directory. Plan A §5 declares section_depends_on on plan B §3, where B §3 is not done. The roadmap lists A §2 among the ready, dispatchable sections and keeps A §5 out with a blocker naming B §3. It fails at the base revision, with that arm logged, and passes at the head. A second case shows that a plan with no mapping blocks exactly as before.\n\ntests/test_schema.py covers the mapping's round-trip through the plan HTML meta, and a refusal for a reference to a section the target plan does not declare.\n\nThe negative control drops the mapping from the roadmap's blocker computation in a scratch copy. The ready-set case then fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line.\n\nThe gate `/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_roadmap.py tests/test_schema.py` exits 0 from the worktree, or shows no added failures by id against the base. The tests never read the real mounted projects.",
    "estimated_hours": 6.0,
    "goal": "Plan dependency-edge-semantics, followup f-des-source-section-depends (read it in docs/plans/dependency-edge-semantics.html near its followups; it recommends /reckon-build dependency-edge-semantics §4). Today a dependency's source is always the whole plan. So one section that must wait for another plan's section hides every other section of its plan from the ready set.\n\nAdd a `section_depends_on` mapping beside `section_declarations`, so that a named section can wait on another plan's section while its sibling sections stay dispatchable. The roadmap then blocks only the named sections, and `read_plan`'s deps resolve each section reference.\n\nFollow the plan's locked decisions honour-the-anchor and one-edge-with-transition. Keep the existing whole-plan depends_on behaviour unchanged for plans that do not declare the mapping.",
